# clangd configuration for the Lin project.
#
# build.bash compiles with MSYS2 MinGW g++, whose default target is
# x86_64-w64-windows-gnu. clangd, however, defaults to x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
# and rejects MinGW flags outright (it errors with
# "unsupported option '-mconsole' for target 'x86_64-pc-windows-msvc'"),
# which breaks windows.h resolution and produces phantom errors in Helix.
#
# Setting the target here aligns clangd with the real build. Paired with the
# --query-driver flag in %APPDATA%\helix\languages.toml, clangd then asks g++
# for its system include paths, so no hardcoded -isystem entries are needed.
CompileFlags:
  Add: [--target=x86_64-w64-windows-gnu]